id: pm-j36ypd
title: "GH-679: linked-test output capture must not abort verbose child tools with EAGAIN"
description: "GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/679 reports that verbose child output can exhaust nonblocking capture and abort with EAGAIN. Bound and drain output while retaining deterministic evidence and token efficiency."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-25T02:06:33.533Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T06:27:18.319Z"
author: unknown
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Linked-test execution drains child stdout/stderr continuously so verbose tools cannot exhaust the capture buffer or receive EAGAIN; Captured evidence remains deterministic and bounded, with any truncation disclosed in the recorded test result rather than silently dropped; A regression test runs a deliberately high-volume child command and asserts completion plus bounded evidence"
parent: pm-usfg
